?mibextid=wwXIfr","createdAt":"2025-11-15T19:36:52.000Z","createdAtUnix":1763235412,"createdAtLabel":null,"language":"en","conversationId":"1989779655822651800","inReplyToStatusId":null,"inReplyToUserId":null,"inReplyToScreenName":null,"quotedStatusId":null,"retweetTweetId":null,"author":{"handle":"CoachBeede","displayName":"Coach Beede","avatarUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2063659131026788352/AE8IYAiH_400x400.jpg","profileUrl":"https://x.com/CoachBeede","verified":false,"blueVerified":true,"platformUserId":"262857654","bio":"Coach Beede, helping families since 1987. Guiding families through the athletic and academic process. Join the Clubhouse at https://t.co/ZRqGb094Qd","location":"Boston","website":"https://CoachBeede.com","bannerUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/262857654/1780849733/1500x500","accountCreatedAt":"2011-03-08T22:22:00.000Z","privateAccount":false,"verifiedType":null,"affiliateLabel":null,"professional":{"type":"Creator","category":[{"id":800,"name":"Sports, Fitness & Recreation","icon_name":"IconBriefcaseStroke"}],"restId":"1468598668643082243"},"metrics":{"availableFields":["followers","following","tweets","favourites","listedCount","mediaCount"],"followers":50087,"following":13162,"tweets":49329,"favourites":161839,"listedCount":99,"mediaCount":3680}},"metrics":{"availableFields":["likes","retweets","replies","quotes","views","bookmarkCount"],"likes":17,"retweets":4,"replies":1,"quotes":1,"views":7414,"bookmarkCount":2},"media":[],"expandedUrl":"https://www.facebook.com/share/v/1Gs1LAfTYv/?mibextid=wwXIfr","isRetweet":false,"isReply":false,"isQuote":false,"source":"Twitter for iPhone","communityId":null,"hasAIGeneratedMedia":false,"isPaidPromotion":false,"isTranslatable":false,"hasBirdwatchNotes":false,"possiblySensitive":false,"entities":{"hashtags":[],"userMentions":[{"handle":"bsblbluebook","displayName":"Bluebook Sports™","platformUserId":"251408354"}],"urls":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/share/v/1Gs1LAfTYv/?mibextid=wwXIfr","displayUrl":"https://www.facebook.com/share/v/1Gs1LAfTYv/?mibextid=wwXIfr","expandedUrl":"https://www.facebook.com/share/v/1Gs1LAfTYv/?mibextid=wwXIfr"}],"symbols":[]},"card":null,"poll":null,"article":null,"place":null,"communityNote":null,"isEdited":false,"quotedTweet":null,"retweetedTweet":null},{"id":"1989370960437473488","url":"https://x.com/coachdrew94/status/1989370960437473488","text":"Prospect Camps: What Parents Need to Know\n\nParents often ask me whether their son should attend a prospect camp. My answer always starts with one key question: Is the camp school‑specific, or is it open‑ended with a lot of different coaches?\n\nSchool‑specific camps are my preference. Why? Because your son gets direct exposure to the coaches at that school without being lost in a sea of competition. It’s focused, targeted, and far more valuable.\n\nMulti‑school camps can also be worthwhile, but only if the schools are aligned — either in the same conference (like the Ivy League) or on the same academic/athletic level. That way, your son is showcasing himself to programs that truly fit his profile.\n\nUnknown or unfocused camps are where I draw the line. If I don’t know the schools involved, I won’t recommend them. Sending your son blindly into a camp without clarity on who’s watching is a waste of time, money, and opportunity.\n\nThe bottom line: Prospect camps can be powerful tools, but only when they’re strategic. The right camp puts your son in front of the right coaches, at the right level, with the right opportunities. Anything else is just noise.","createdAt":"2025-11-14T16:32:52.000Z","createdAtUnix":1763137972,"createdAtLabel":null,"language":"en","conversationId":"1989370960437473488","inReplyToStatusId":null,"inReplyToUserId":null,"inReplyToScreenName":null,"quotedStatusId":null,"retweetTweetId":null,"author":{"handle":"coachdrew94","displayName":"Coach Drew's Recruiting Service - 27 yrs. exp.","avatarUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2117681283660996608/wjkYgCjw_400x400.jpg","profileUrl":"https://x.com/coachdrew94","verified":false,"blueVerified":true,"platformUserId":"1667193117597143040","bio":"If you're a 27' player with 0 offers, still looking, not ready to give up, I can help you find offers. https://t.co/KBP0klXNsL","location":"Serving families nationwide","website":"https://coachdrew93.com/","bannerUrl":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1667193117597143040/1793728987/1500x500","accountCreatedAt":"2023-06-09T15:33:27.000Z","privateAccount":false,"verifiedType":null,"affiliateLabel":null,"professional":null,"metrics":{"availableFields":["followers","following","tweets","favourites","listedCount","mediaCount"],"followers":16335,"following":7408,"tweets":4435,"favourites":15,"listedCount":5,"mediaCount":146}},"metrics":{"availableFields":["likes","retweets","replies","quotes","views","bookmarkCount"],"likes":2,"retweets":1,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"views":1262,"bookmarkCount":2},"media":[],"expandedUrl":null,"isRetweet":false,"isReply":false,"isQuote":false,"source":null,"communityId":null,"hasAIGeneratedMedia":false,"isPaidPromotion":false,"isTranslatable":false,"hasBirdwatchNotes":false,"possiblySensitive":false,"entities":{"hashtags":[],"userMentions":[],"urls":[],"symbols":[]},"card":null,"poll":null,"article":null,"place":null,"communityNote":null,"isEdited":false,"quotedTweet":null,"retweetedTweet":null},{"id":"1950966620697813358","url":"https://x.com/coachdrew94/status/1950966620697813358","text":"If you’re a 27’ or younger player going to generic showcases you and your parents have no idea what you’re doing. It is a waste of time and money. Your chances of impressing a coach is less than 5%. If you’re in that 1-5% category, then go. If not, work on your strength, speed, skills and GRADES. Next year you’ll increase your chances and maybe the coach likes what he sees. Coach Drew","createdAt":"2025-07-31T17:07:44.000Z","createdAtUnix":1753981664,"createdAtLabel":null,"language":"en","conversat